      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>W. P. HARTLEY'S</head>
        <p>W. P. HARTLEY'S</p>
        <p>Seville Orange MARMALADE is absolutely pure.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON TO QUARRY OWNERS. 1 The Paving and Sewerage Committee of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive Tenders for 2,000 tons of tin. Granite or Whinstone Cubes. Specifications, and all further information may be obtained at the othce of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on .and after Moadsy next the 11th instant, at which place tended' must be delivered before 10 o'clock a.m. on Monday, the 25th day of September. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. THOMAS LONGDIN, Borough Engineer and Surveyor. Borough Engineer and Surveyor's Office, September Bth, 1911. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— HALL KEEPER AND WIFE WANTED. The Corporation of Warrington require the services of a Man ani his Wife (without children) to take charge of the Town Hall. Joint salary, 353. per week, with roomy, coal, gaa, de., in the Town Hall, and uniform. Candidates most be between 24 and 45 yeari of age. Applications, accompanied by copies of three testimonials of recent data (on forms which will Le supplied by the undersigned on receipt of stamped addressed envelope) roust be sent to me on or before Saturday, the 30th day of September instant. A list of the duties to be performed will be supplied. Canvass- ing the members of the Council after this date will disqualify any candidate. Dated this Bth September, 1911. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk. Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
        <p>LANGLANDS' SAILINGS to GREENOCK and GLASGOW. " PRINCESS LOUISE " or other STEAMER From LIVERPOOL From GLASGOW. (Clarence dock). (Berths Nos. 22-28 North side) Tues. Sept. 12,12 noon Sat. Sept. 9, 3 p.m. *9.30 p.m. Sot. Sept. 16,3 p.m. Thurs. Sept 14,3 p.m.* 7.10 p.m, Thurs. Sept. "1, 9 p.m. Tues. Sept. 19, 3 p.m. *8.30 p.m. *Train fromlasgow (Central) to Greenock (Central) SPECIAL REDUCED THROUGH TICKETS from Warrington, &amp;c. Single, Ist clam &amp; saloon 1300 d. ; 3rd class &amp; saloon 12s. 6d. ; 3rd class &amp; steerage 7s. Return (valid for two months) 3rd class &amp; saloon 19s. I SPECIAL 10 DAYS EXCURSION TICKETS: 3rd class &amp; saloon 16s. 6d. 3rd class &amp; steerage On. 6d. M. LANGLANDS &amp; SONS, 14, CROSS STREET, MANCHESTER. BROWN'S BUILDINGS, EXCHANGE, LIVERPOOL DUBLIN ALSO E 4111,1" vkr." TEDCASTLE LINE. S.S. "BLACEROCK," "CUMBRIA," " EBL ANA," and " ADELA," from SOUTH Side, NELSON DOCK, Liverpool. Every Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday and Saturday, to DUBLIN. Return Saloon, 10s.; Steerage 1.. with Cheap Excursion Tickets EVERY SAILING, DAY, to Bray, Wicklow, Avoca, &amp;c., and on Fridass and Saturdays to Killarney,Cork,Bundoran, Warrenpoint,&amp;c. Fast S.S."BLACKROCK" every Tuesday and Friday from Liverpool, and Mondays and Wednesdays from Dublin. SPECIAL SIX DAYS' SEA CRUISE, per "Cumbria." Every Saturday, to Whiteharen, giving 3 days for English Lakes, thence to Dublin, and back to Liverpool (6 days or within 2 months). Saloon 223. 6d. or with le meals, 21s. additional. Apply TEDCASTLE, McCORMICK A CO., LTD Liverpool. Telegrams " Tedoastle." Telephone 975</p>
