      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <head>Sales by Auction.</head>
        <p>Sales by Auction.</p>
        <p>rit 0 BE SOLD BY AUCTION By Messrs. JOHN MAINWARING &amp; CO., on Tuesday, 19th September, 1911, at 3 p.m. prompt, at the Patten Arms Hotel, Warrington, the following , FREEHOLD PROPERTIES, situate at THELWALL, Cheshire, about three miles from Warringtoo,and about 14 miles from Manchester :- LOT 1.-A FARM HOUSE, known as the Bridge Farm, with good and extensive farm buildings and land, comprising a total area of 44a. Ir. 37p. or thereabouts. Near thelwall Station, and has frontages on high roads and on the Bridgewater Canal. Lox 2.-A plot of Building LAND situate in Waste- lane and Halfscre-lane, containing 4a. Ir. 3p. or there- abouts. LOT 3.-A plot of Building LAND approached by a private road off Halfacre-lane, containing 4a, Or. 21p. or thereabouts. LOT 4.-A plot of Building LAND situate on a private road off Halfacre-lane, containing sa. Ir. 37p. or thereabouts, having a frontage on the Bridgewater Canal. Lots 2,9, and 4 are all near Thelwall Station. LOT 5.-A COTTAGE and GARDEN, Weighing Machine, Coalyard, Office and Stable, adjacent to Thelwall Station. LOT 6.-Two Semi-detached COTTAGES with good Gardens, occupied by Messrs. Hampton and Bowker. Also Wheelwright's and Blacksmith's Shops and Shoeing Forge, in the occupation of Hampton Bros. All situate in Thelicall Village, on the main birth road. LOT 7.-A good HOUSE, outbuildings, garden and croft, part in the occupation of Mr. Scragg, and part in band, situate on the main high road In Thelwall Village. Area is. Sr. 26p. or thereabouts. Lox 8.-Valuable Building LAND comprising part of Thelwall Hall Park and other land with a cottage sad garden. This lot lies between two main high roads with ample frontages to each. Area, 325, Or. 23p. or thereabouts. LOT 9.-Valuable LANDS for works, situate on the north side of and adjacent to the Manchester Ship Canal. Area. 37a. Sr. 16p. or thereabouts. LOT 10.-Valuable LAND for works, situate on the north side of the Manchester Ship Canal, and adjoining the river Mersey. Area, 16a. Ir. 23p., or thereabouts. LOT 11.-A Small HOLDING, comprising House, Farm Buildings, and Land adjacent to the Manchester Ship Canal, and having along building frontage to the Thelwall high road, now in the occupation of Mr. Arthur Morris. Area, 15a. Or. Bp. or thereabouts. Lox 12.-Two good FIELDS, adjacent to the Man- chester Ship Canal now iii the occupation of Mr. Arthur Morris and Mr. C. H. Lloyd. Ares, Ida, lr. 11p, or thereabouts. LOT 13.-Two Semi-detached COTTAGES and Gardens, known as Nos. 5 and 6, Sweet Pea Cottages, near Thelwall Station, in the occupation of Messrs Ward and Sudd. These are modern houses with three bedrooms and bath. LOT 14.-Two Semi-detache 1 COTTAGES and Gardens, known as Nos. :1 end 4, Sweet Pea Cottages, near Thelwall Station, la the occupation of Messrs. Rite and Brookes. These are modern houses, with three bedrooms and baths. Lo r 15.-Two Semi-detached _COTTAGES and Gerdens, known as NOII. 1 and 2, Sweet Pea Cottages, sear Thelwall Station, now in the ocanpation of Messrs. Rite and Richardson. Thule are good modern houses, with three bedrooms. LOT 16.-Two Semi-detached COTTAGES with Out- buildings and large Gardens, in the occupation of Mrs. Davenport, and Mr. Phceni. This lot is near Thelwall Station with along (rootage to the highroad. LOT 17.-Two Semi-detached COTTAGES with good Gardens in the occupation of Messrs George Lambert and George Ainsworth, situate in Bell-lane, within 3 minutes' walk from Thelwall Station. Area, Ir. 19p. or thereabouts. The above properties will be offered, *abject to con- ditions of sale to be then read, in the first instance in one Lot, and if not so sold then in the above Lots. For particulars and plans, apply to the Auctioneers, Bridge-street; Messrs. John Allite and Co., Surveyors, Bold-street) or MOWS. ROBERT DAVIES and Co., Solicitors, Market-place, Warrington.</p>
        <p>MOW. Sold or Let.—Two Modern SEMI-DETACHED VILLAS containing 4 bedrooms, Box Room, large dining and drawing-room, bath-room, w.c. etc., ball I 2 ft. square, with all the up-to-date modern conveniences, will be let or sold singly or in pairs. 4-5 of the purchase money con remain on at i per cent. if datired.—Apply W. FITRNSSS, Great Sankey.</p>
        <p>I DEAL HOMES by Matthews and Bennetts are now I. being erected at Bowes Park, one of the prettiest and healthiest suburbs in the North of London. They contain diningroom, with timbered ceiling and panelled walls, drawingroom, lounge hall with oak parquet door, kitchen, scullery, and usual ofnces, 4 good bedrooms, bathroom with tiled risor and walls, hand c, shower \ bath, hot towel rail, w.c tiled out, hoes cupboard, tr.c. Houses overlook permanent gardens, all road charges paid, price £490, low ground rent, essay terms.—Apply Of Call OD the ESTATE, Bounds Green rd. (opposite Warwick rd. , smin. Bowie Park Statiwi, G.N.R.</p>
        <p>IT WAS LIKE MAGIC !</p>
