        <p>ALBERT CLEAVE V. ALL. SCaTr. This was an excellent Oral, the only blemish on the game was that it termineled in the moonlight. Co u- mencing the game at 6-23 it took an hour and forty minutes to bring about the result. Albert Gleevs in this 'ear's winner of the Manchester and District Individual Merit Campetition and repregents Bole Head while Alfred Scott of the Cemetery has achieved some floe performances in the county games. BY.L stepped on the tooter full of coofidence. It looked a I good thing for (Heave at IS-12. Handkerchiefs had to be applied to discern the bl_ck, Scgtt capturiog the blo, k which is a lot in ale player's favour. He came along wits arms oft, the game bgiog then IS all, subsequently 20 all. Scott with the block in bond played towards the entragce, and there win great excite- ment the spectators ',curing on the green to ace the final end. It was a remarkable end, and fitting for the occasion, when one must consider that it was the last wood to be played in the Individual Merit Ccrtpetition that decided the winner. Scott by up, ahout a yard and half away. Cleave came along and drew the end which made him champion for the MB= 1911.</p>
        <p>GREEN-WOOD.</p>
