      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0081" n="art0081">
        <head>SEA-WATER CURE FOR INFANTILE CHOLERA.</head>
        <p>SEA-WATER CURE FOR INFANTILE CHOLERA.</p>
        <p>• • t 1 - 44, 4 E. • .1 , + a , t • e. , • •</p>
        <p>There has recently bern opened in London a charitable dispensary, the Quinton Polyclinic, fcr treating infantile cholera by sca-watcr. The treatment consists of hypodermic injections el carefully prepared doses ot modified sea-water into the soft tissues of the skin between the shoulders. Already hundreds of lives have been saved. The treatment is the invention of a Frenchman, M. Quinton. Our picture shows a nurse iniectino the tea-water by means of the special apparatus.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0082" n="art0082">
        <head>LONDON'S NEW OPERA HOUSE</head>
        <p>LONDON'S NEW OPERA HOUSE</p>
        <p>- - _ The Londcn Cpera House, which is being built by Mr. Oscar Hammerstein, is nearing completion, and is to be opened early in November. It is a magnificent structure, standing at the Strand end of Kingsway. It occupns 26,400 square feet and has four street frontages. Mr. Hammerstein is busy at the present time making preparations for the staging of operas at his new house. He has experts travelling all over the Continent searching for talent, and is having the scenery, costumes, &amp;c.. of thirty operas prepared at a cost of between £5,000 and £lO.OOO each</p>
        <p>• • 4,00. Weti f=„ , 7 73 8 1411 .t • • " • -• ) , . .</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>KING EDWARD'S NEWMARKET HOME.</head>
        <p>KING EDWARD'S NEWMARKET HOME.</p>
        <p>Grafion House, Newmarket, with two and a-half acres of ground, which formerly belonged to King Edward, has been purchased by Sir Ernest Cassel and presented to the people of Newmarket for use as an open space. The gift has been gratefully accepted, as the want of an open space for the public has long been felt.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0084" n="art0084">
        <head>BABY'S SKIN ITCHED AND BURNED.</head>
        <p>BABY'S SKIN ITCHED AND BURNED.</p>
