        <p>NORTH-WESTERN.</p>
        <p>Observation cars are run on many foreign railways every day, and there are a few things that add more to the clia.rn of a journey through beautiful country then to sit at one's 0111941 in the luxurious vehicles provided and watch the surrounding country unfold itself es the train journeys along. Lugs plate-giass windows at the sides and ends of the carriage enable passengers to view the poising sceaely without that vexations neck-craning whit h is entailed in an or Navy compartment, and It is gratifying to leers that the L. and N.-W. R.," The Premier Line," is shout to introduce them. Arrange- Ccclv ore being made for a vehicle of this description t o a small extra charge the magnificent scenery of the C 'nary Valley will be shown to the passenger from many different aspects.</p>
