      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0130" n="art0130">
        <head>SPECIAL PRIZES.</head>
        <p>SPECIAL PRIZES.</p>
        <p>CORONATIoN PRIZE.—For the best display of flowers, foliage or plants used in the way of decorations of the front of any building on Coronation Day. Presented by his Worship the Mayor (Dr , Joseph) : 2, T Williams and &amp;a, Parker-street Fronts or backs of premises.—The best display of creepers or growing plants on front or hack of a private house : 1 and 2, divided S Baldry, 125, Church-street, S Williams ; 3, F H Robinson. The best display of creepers or growing plants on the front or book of shop or other business premises : I, E Junes, 106, Butter- ' market-street ; 2, Mrs Chrimes, Roe Buck Hotel, Bridge. street. By the owners of the houses Nos. 31 to 77, 18 and 20, Wakstield-street (per Mr A H Clive), to the tenants of those houses for the beet kept and stocked front garden : 1,1 M Platt, No 20; 2, N F Seymour No. 47 ; 3, G H Hussey, No. 53; 4,51 E Naylor, No. 61 By the owner of the houses Nos. 95 to 43, and 47 toil, Willis-street (per Mr. Stansfleld), to the tenants of those houses for the best kept and stocked front Cr back garden : E Glent on, No. 37. To the tenants of houses Nos. 20 to 36 Parr-street (per Mr J H Gittens) for the best kept and stocked front garden: I, T E .n, No 26 : 2, A H Racey, No 21.</p>
        <p>N), lORIA P RK ALLOTLIFAT GARDFNS.—For the best kept and best stocked allotment garden in Victoria Park. rrownted by J Lyon Whittle : I, John Woods (No 20) : 2„I T Cooper (No ; Lharles Ward (No 25).</p>
